{"id": "EUVD-2026-76497", "enisaUuid": "dbbc6b8b-62e7-3daf-a714-403ba4f6b7b2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nauxdisplay: charlcd: cancel backlight work on registration failure\n\nWith CONFIG_CHARLCD_BL_FLASH, charlcd_init() schedules bl_work before\ncharlcd_register() calls misc_register(). If registration fails, the\ncaller frees the charlcd object while delayed work still contains its\naddress.\n\nAdd charlcd_deinit() to cancel the delayed work and turn the backlight\noff. Use it for both registration rollback and normal unregistration.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:17", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cd97b3c68fe3c06c8067cc59d7dff976c5b7ea04", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22586432c1aba89d9bd33f3173408dac830f220b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6eaed64a32e550daf0dc9549742b3ab9e41d984f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fe7ba73dde94c5f413b1588cd444b49105015dda", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/84858671842ae5857b9ed1202b62f9045373dcd1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff2fb3c1e60cb247ea3e28c0ea0bea81c18f7755", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3e3bf40916c1e810df03958cfa7ba6883cdce79"], "aliases": ["GHSA-72rp-5pw2-wrgc", "CVE-2026-89585"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0363fb63-3ed0-3945-9783-717ef65433ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "39f8ea46724efbed3ca021863a22337c31be264c <cd97b3c68fe3c06c8067cc59d7dff976c5b7ea04"}, {"id": "10897f6d-c4bc-34d7-869c-129631d43555", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "39f8ea46724efbed3ca021863a22337c31be264c <ff2fb3c1e60cb247ea3e28c0ea0bea81c18f7755"}, {"id": "16e65fc7-0711-3112-ae51-696d2bc90ac2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "